1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,337
Hi!

3
00:00:04,387 --> 00:00:06,415
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,536 --> 00:00:11,767
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,079 --> 00:00:15,504
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,554 --> 00:00:18,415
The Ugly Duckling Who Became a Swan!

7
00:00:22,994 --> 00:00:28,263
Once upon a time, on a sunny farm, there
was a summer so lovely that the wheat

8
00:00:28,313 --> 00:00:32,352
shone like gold and the
hay smelled like honey.

9
00:00:34,894 --> 00:00:39,336
Near a quiet pond, hidden
under some enormous leaves,

10
00:00:39,408 --> 00:00:43,156
Mother Duck was waiting, with
all the patience in the world,

11
00:00:43,228 --> 00:00:45,031
for her eggs to hatch.

12
00:00:45,682 --> 00:00:51,410
Popcorn the owl, who loved visiting the
farm, was perched on the wooden fence,

13
00:00:51,460 --> 00:00:53,721
counting the eggs one by one.

14
00:00:54,315 --> 00:00:55,691
Hoo, hoo!

15
00:00:55,835 --> 00:01:01,416
Five of the eggs are small and pale,
but that last one is enormous and grey!

16
00:01:01,466 --> 00:01:05,129
Popcorn said, her eyes wide open.

17
00:01:05,777 --> 00:01:10,880
One fine day, there was a crack, and
then another, and out of the small eggs

18
00:01:10,930 --> 00:01:15,094
came five yellow ducklings,
fluffy and noisy.

19
00:01:15,771 --> 00:01:20,227
How big and beautiful the world is,
look at all those green leaves up there!

20
00:01:20,277 --> 00:01:24,205
the brothers and sisters
said, blinking at the sun.

21
00:01:24,860 --> 00:01:29,935
But the big grey egg stayed closed, and
Mother Duck had to wait one more day,

22
00:01:29,985 --> 00:01:31,190
and then another.

23
00:01:31,739 --> 00:01:36,383
This egg is taking so long, but I am a
mother, and a mother always waits with

24
00:01:36,433 --> 00:01:37,630
lots of love,

25
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:40,788
Mother Duck said, fluffing her feathers.

26
00:01:41,419 --> 00:01:46,953
At last, the big egg cracked open,
and out came a duckling unlike all the

27
00:01:47,003 --> 00:01:48,008
others:

28
00:01:48,058 --> 00:01:52,486
big, grey, with a long
neck and enormous feet.

29
00:01:53,104 --> 00:01:56,777
The yellow brothers and sisters
looked at him and started whispering,

30
00:01:56,827 --> 00:02:00,046
because they had never seen
a duck like that before.

31
00:02:00,613 --> 00:02:04,658
He is different, but he is my
son, and his name will be Dusty,

32
00:02:04,708 --> 00:02:08,831
Mother Duck said, touching
his head gently with her beak.

33
00:02:09,918 --> 00:02:14,040
The next day, Mother Duck took
all her ducklings to the pond,

34
00:02:14,098 --> 00:02:17,137
and jumped into the
water with a big splash.

35
00:02:19,324 --> 00:02:24,274
One by one, the ducklings jumped
in after her, and Dusty did too,

36
00:02:24,324 --> 00:02:28,982
and he swam better than all of them,
with strong feet and a nice straight

37
00:02:29,032 --> 00:02:30,232
neck.

38
00:02:30,444 --> 00:02:34,144
Just look how well he swims, and
how straight he holds his neck,

39
00:02:34,194 --> 00:02:35,761
he really is my son,

40
00:02:35,811 --> 00:02:38,308
Mother Duck said, very proudly.

41
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:43,535
Then Mother Duck took the family to the
farmyard, to introduce the ducklings

42
00:02:43,585 --> 00:02:45,165
to the other animals.

43
00:02:45,832 --> 00:02:50,032
There were the hens, the other
ducks and a very vain turkey,

44
00:02:50,082 --> 00:02:53,024
and they all stared at Dusty in surprise.

45
00:02:53,569 --> 00:02:57,651
What a strange duckling, so big and so
grey, he does not look like a real duck

46
00:02:57,701 --> 00:02:58,365
at all,

47
00:02:58,415 --> 00:03:01,510
the turkey said, puffing up his feathers.

48
00:03:02,153 --> 00:03:06,992
The yellow brothers and sisters began
to laugh and copy the way Dusty walked,

49
00:03:07,042 --> 00:03:09,748
and even the older ducks giggled.

50
00:03:10,371 --> 00:03:14,229
You are too big and too grey,
Dusty, go and play somewhere else,

51
00:03:14,279 --> 00:03:17,860
the brothers and sisters said,
with their beaks in the air.

52
00:03:18,503 --> 00:03:22,875
Dusty hung his head, and went
to hide behind an old bucket,

53
00:03:22,961 --> 00:03:25,417
feeling a heavy ache in his heart.

54
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:30,064
Popcorn flew down from the fence
and landed right beside him,

55
00:03:30,137 --> 00:03:31,814
without making a sound.

56
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:40,170
Hoo, hoo, please don't be sad,
Dusty, being different is not a flaw,

57
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:42,473
it is just a new way of being,

58
00:03:42,523 --> 00:03:45,785
Popcorn said, in a gentle voice.

59
00:03:46,410 --> 00:03:50,203
But nobody wants to play with me, Popcorn,
and everybody laughs at me all day

60
00:03:50,253 --> 00:03:50,865
long,

61
00:03:50,915 --> 00:03:54,579
Dusty answered, his eyes full of tears.

62
00:03:55,653 --> 00:03:59,566
Early the next morning, while
the sun was still rising,

63
00:03:59,708 --> 00:04:04,025
Dusty quietly left the
farm, without waking anyone.

64
00:04:04,719 --> 00:04:09,128
He crossed the field, slipped under the
fence, and walked until he reached a

65
00:04:09,178 --> 00:04:12,439
huge marsh, full of tall reeds.

66
00:04:15,338 --> 00:04:20,301
Some wild ducks lived there, with
brown feathers and green heads,

67
00:04:20,351 --> 00:04:22,751
and they looked at him with curiosity.

68
00:04:23,415 --> 00:04:26,867
You are quite different, friend,
but you seem to have a kind heart,

69
00:04:26,917 --> 00:04:28,850
and you may stay here as long as you like,

70
00:04:28,900 --> 00:04:30,591
the wild ducks said.

71
00:04:31,243 --> 00:04:36,310
Dusty was very happy, and he spent
many days swimming among the reeds,

72
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:39,935
eating seeds and watching
the clouds drift by.

73
00:04:40,589 --> 00:04:46,442
But one afternoon, the sky grew dark,
and a huge clap of thunder rolled over

74
00:04:46,492 --> 00:04:47,692
the marsh.

75
00:04:54,427 --> 00:04:58,571
The wild ducks flew off all
together, to find a safer place,

76
00:04:58,621 --> 00:05:03,646
and Dusty, who could not fly
yet, stayed hidden in the reeds.

77
00:05:04,274 --> 00:05:08,159
I will not be afraid, the rain will
pass, and tomorrow the sun will come out

78
00:05:08,209 --> 00:05:08,845
again,

79
00:05:08,895 --> 00:05:12,184
Dusty said, curled up under the leaves.

80
00:05:12,802 --> 00:05:15,146
And that is exactly what happened:

81
00:05:15,196 --> 00:05:20,290
the rain passed, the sun came
back, and Dusty went on his way,

82
00:05:20,390 --> 00:05:22,124
braver than before.

83
00:05:23,215 --> 00:05:27,693
When the leaves began to turn
yellow, Dusty came to an old,

84
00:05:27,743 --> 00:05:32,185
crooked wooden cottage,
where a kind old lady lived.

85
00:05:32,832 --> 00:05:38,504
The door was half open, and inside,
near the stove, there were a striped cat

86
00:05:38,554 --> 00:05:43,495
and a round, vain hen, both
very pleased with themselves.

87
00:05:44,103 --> 00:05:47,727
And you, can you lay an egg
every morning, the way I do?

88
00:05:47,777 --> 00:05:50,899
the hen asked, looking Dusty up and down.

89
00:05:51,542 --> 00:05:54,097
No, I cannot lay eggs, Madam Hen,

90
00:05:54,147 --> 00:05:56,242
Dusty answered politely.

91
00:05:56,861 --> 00:06:01,000
And can you purr, or arch your back,
or make sparks fly from your fur when

92
00:06:01,050 --> 00:06:02,457
someone strokes you?

93
00:06:02,507 --> 00:06:04,921
the cat asked, licking his paw.

94
00:06:06,947 --> 00:06:11,052
No, I cannot do that either, but I love
to swim, and to dip my head into the

95
00:06:11,102 --> 00:06:13,942
cool water, it is the
best feeling in the world,

96
00:06:13,992 --> 00:06:16,614
Dusty said, his eyes shining.

97
00:06:17,254 --> 00:06:21,511
What a strange idea, who would ever want
to get their head wet in cold water?

98
00:06:21,561 --> 00:06:24,488
the hen said, laughing out loud.

99
00:06:25,135 --> 00:06:28,993
You do not understand me, and that is
all right, everyone has their own way,

100
00:06:29,043 --> 00:06:32,110
Dusty said, saying goodbye kindly.

101
00:06:32,756 --> 00:06:35,776
And he walked out of the
door with his head held high,

102
00:06:35,826 --> 00:06:40,545
because he had already learned that he
did not have to be like everyone else.

103
00:06:41,622 --> 00:06:47,308
One autumn evening, under an orange
and purple sky, Dusty was swimming on a

104
00:06:47,358 --> 00:06:51,883
quiet lake, when he heard a
beautiful sound high above.

105
00:06:52,543 --> 00:06:57,965
It was a flock of enormous white
birds, with long necks and wide wings,

106
00:06:58,015 --> 00:07:00,526
flying away to the warm countries.

107
00:07:01,156 --> 00:07:05,690
They were swans, and they were the most
beautiful birds Dusty had ever seen in

108
00:07:05,740 --> 00:07:07,001
his whole life.

109
00:07:07,599 --> 00:07:10,043
Hoo, hoo, how lovely!

110
00:07:10,128 --> 00:07:14,834
They are flying far away, to
places where winter never comes,

111
00:07:14,884 --> 00:07:19,131
Popcorn said, perched on a
log at the edge of the lake.

112
00:07:19,786 --> 00:07:24,667
Dusty stretched his neck as high as he
could, and let out such a strange cry

113
00:07:24,717 --> 00:07:27,061
that he even startled himself.

114
00:07:27,710 --> 00:07:31,468
I do not know why, Popcorn, but
I feel like I know those birds,

115
00:07:31,518 --> 00:07:33,070
and I wish I could fly with them,

116
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:37,450
Dusty said, watching the sky
until the swans were gone.

117
00:07:38,570 --> 00:07:43,118
Then winter came, and with it a cold
so bitter that the water of the lake

118
00:07:43,168 --> 00:07:44,790
began to freeze.

119
00:07:44,940 --> 00:07:49,904
Dusty swam around and around, without
stopping, to keep the water from

120
00:07:49,954 --> 00:07:53,674
freezing, but the open
space kept getting smaller.

121
00:07:54,299 --> 00:07:59,971
One icy morning, his feet got stuck in
the ice, and he could not move from his

122
00:08:00,021 --> 00:08:01,221
spot.

123
00:08:01,558 --> 00:08:06,389
Just then, a kind farmer
walked by, with a red wool cap,

124
00:08:06,461 --> 00:08:09,194
a brown beard and a blue coat.

125
00:08:09,825 --> 00:08:14,284
Well, well, a poor bird stuck
in the ice, let me help you,

126
00:08:14,334 --> 00:08:18,470
the farmer said, carefully
breaking the ice with his boot.

127
00:08:19,154 --> 00:08:23,923
He wrapped Dusty in his scarf and carried
him home, where the fire was lit and

128
00:08:23,973 --> 00:08:26,234
the children came running to see.

129
00:08:26,873 --> 00:08:31,643
The children wanted to play, but
Dusty got scared, flapped his wings,

130
00:08:31,693 --> 00:08:34,884
and landed right inside the bowl of flour!

131
00:08:35,554 --> 00:08:40,524
He came out white from his head to his
toes, and everyone burst out laughing,

132
00:08:40,721 --> 00:08:42,468
even Dusty himself.

133
00:08:43,122 --> 00:08:47,901
You can stay in the barn until spring,
my friend, there is warm straw there

134
00:08:47,951 --> 00:08:49,693
and nobody will bother you,

135
00:08:49,743 --> 00:08:51,837
the farmer said, smiling.

136
00:08:52,483 --> 00:08:57,758
And so Dusty spent the whole
winter in the barn, warm and safe,

137
00:08:57,830 --> 00:09:01,647
listening to the wind outside
and dreaming about the swans.

138
00:09:02,736 --> 00:09:08,255
When spring arrived, the sun grew warm
again, and the apple trees were covered

139
00:09:08,305 --> 00:09:10,038
in pink blossoms.

140
00:09:10,670 --> 00:09:15,292
Dusty opened his wings, and noticed
that they were big and strong,

141
00:09:15,545 --> 00:09:17,681
much stronger than before.

142
00:09:18,369 --> 00:09:23,833
He flapped his wings once, twice, and
suddenly he was flying over the fields,

143
00:09:23,883 --> 00:09:26,213
for the very first time in his life!

144
00:09:29,849 --> 00:09:33,744
He flew to an enormous garden
with a blue lake, and there,

145
00:09:33,794 --> 00:09:38,666
swimming very slowly, were
three beautiful white swans.

146
00:09:39,293 --> 00:09:44,118
Dusty landed on the water, lowered his
head, and thought the swans would laugh

147
00:09:44,168 --> 00:09:47,096
at him, just like everyone else.

148
00:09:47,714 --> 00:09:51,706
But when he looked down at the
water, he saw his reflection,

149
00:09:51,756 --> 00:09:54,781
and he could hardly believe his eyes.

150
00:09:55,464 --> 00:09:58,531
He was no longer a clumsy grey duckling:

151
00:09:58,610 --> 00:10:04,032
he was a white swan, elegant, with a
long neck and feathers shining in the

152
00:10:04,082 --> 00:10:05,282
sun!

153
00:10:05,629 --> 00:10:08,420
Welcome, brother, we have
been waiting for you,

154
00:10:08,470 --> 00:10:11,940
the oldest swan said,
swimming over to him.

155
00:10:12,594 --> 00:10:14,929
I was a swan all along, and I never knew,

156
00:10:14,979 --> 00:10:18,768
Dusty said, his voice trembling with joy.

157
00:10:19,892 --> 00:10:24,009
At the edge of the lake, some
children were tossing breadcrumbs,

158
00:10:24,059 --> 00:10:28,334
and a little girl cried out in
delight that a new swan had come,

159
00:10:28,517 --> 00:10:30,834
the most beautiful of them all.

160
00:10:31,447 --> 00:10:36,430
But Dusty did not become proud, because
a good heart never gets too proud.

161
00:10:37,075 --> 00:10:42,053
A few days later, he flew back to the
farm, to visit Mother Duck and his

162
00:10:42,103 --> 00:10:43,947
brothers and sisters.

163
00:10:44,597 --> 00:10:46,601
Dusty, is it really you?

164
00:10:46,805 --> 00:10:50,078
You look so beautiful, and we
were so silly to laugh at you,

165
00:10:50,128 --> 00:10:53,626
the brothers and sisters
said, feeling ashamed.

166
00:10:54,281 --> 00:10:57,935
Everything is forgiven, because now I
know that everyone grows in their own

167
00:10:57,985 --> 00:10:59,888
time, and in their own way,

168
00:10:59,938 --> 00:11:03,074
Dusty said, spreading his white wings.

169
00:11:03,621 --> 00:11:07,733
I always knew you were special, my
son, ever since the day you came out of

170
00:11:07,783 --> 00:11:08,860
that big egg,

171
00:11:08,910 --> 00:11:12,004
Mother Duck said, crying with joy.

172
00:11:12,665 --> 00:11:18,482
And Popcorn, perched on the farm
fence, blinked her big eyes and smiled,

173
00:11:18,568 --> 00:11:22,370
as if she had known the ending of
the story from the very beginning.

174
00:11:29,700 --> 00:11:30,900
The End.

175
00:11:32,615 --> 00:11:33,327
Hoo...

176
00:11:33,377 --> 00:11:34,401
Psst!

177
00:11:34,451 --> 00:11:36,023
Are you still awake?

178
00:11:36,177 --> 00:11:38,231
Did you like tonight's story?

179
00:11:38,352 --> 00:11:43,068
Dusty showed us that being different
is not a flaw, that everyone grows in

180
00:11:43,118 --> 00:11:47,749
their own time, and that kindness
matters much more than looks.

181
00:11:48,092 --> 00:11:52,399
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

182
00:11:52,695 --> 00:11:57,593
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

183
00:11:57,643 --> 00:12:00,048
for more stories at bedtime.

184
00:12:00,352 --> 00:12:01,552
Hoo...

